-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6ChkCx`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem R6Chk.entChk_sound (hbad : bad = BADf n) (hn : n ≤ 24) {kV nH H s : ℕ} (hnk : nH + kV = n)
--       (hH : H < 2 ^ (32 * nH)) (hHr : ∀ i < nH, row H i < 2 ^ n)
--       {SV : Submodule (ZMod 2) (Fin n → ZMod 2)}
--       (hmem : ∀ x, x ∈ SV ↔ ∀ i : Fin nH, vr n H i ⬝ᵥ x = 0) (hV : NondegF SV)
--       (hVd : finrank (ZMod 2) SV = kV) (h : entChk bad kV nH H s = true) :
--       spanP n (tk (nx s) (f32 s)) (f32 s) ≤ SV ∧
--         finrank (ZMod 2) (spanP n (tk (nx s) (f32 s)) (f32 s)) = f32 s ∧
--         NondegF (spanP n (tk (nx s) (f32 s)) (f32 s)) ∧
--         (spanP n (tk (nx s) (f32 s)) (f32 s) = SV ∨
--           ∃ w ∈ SV, w ⬝ᵥ w = 1 ∧ ∀ z ∈ spanP n (tk (nx s) (f32 s)) (f32 s), z ⬝ᵥ w = 0)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Reflective checker for nested nondegenerate `F₂` label pairs (complex round six)
--
--   Data: a list of **groups**. A group is one natural number read as 32-bit fields (LSB first):
--   `kV, cnt, B (kV rows), H (n-kV), D (kV), E (n-kV)`, then `cnt` entries `kU, U (kU), EU (kU),
--   R (kV-kU)`. Rows are vectors of `F₂^n` (`n ≤ 24`).
--
--   * `grpChk n bad G : Bool` — two packed products for the label `V = span B`
--     (`H·[B;E]ᵀ = [0 | I]`, `D·[H;B]ᵀ = [0 | I]`) and two per entry
--     (`U·[H;EU]ᵀ = [0 | I]`, `R·[H;U;R]ᵀ = [0 | 0 | I]`), plus row range checks.
--   * `grpChk_sound`: if `grpChk n (BADf n) G = true` then `V` is nondegenerate of dimension `kV`,
--     and for every entry `(U, kU)`, `PairOK n U kU V kV`: `span U ≤ span V`, `dim span U = kU`,
--     `span U` nondegenerate, and `span U = span V` or some `w ∈ span V` has `w·w = 1`, `w ⊥ U`
--     (i.e. `NetComplexP8.Up (span U) (span V)` with `Fd = kV - kU`; see `R6ChkCxBridge`).
--
